<title>USA: Omaha Public 478 MW Neb. nuke seen on line Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Omaha Public 478 MW Neb. nuke seen on line Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Omaha Public Power District's 478 megawatt Fort Calhoun nuclear power plant will likely resume production Tuesday following scheduled maintenance, a company spokeswoman said Monday.</p>
<p>Startup at the plant had begun as of Monday, and the unit should synchronize to the grid Tuesday, said spokeswoman Delores Jacobberger.</p>
<p>The Fort Calhoun, Neb., unit was shut Oct 5 for refueling and maintenance and is Omaha Public's only nuclear power facility.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
